DXF ORIGIN CONVENTION (our code):
  (0, 0) = bottom-left corner of BLANK
  Y increases upward
  Hard corners (void inner corners) at (el+BD, eb+BD) where el/eb = f1+f2 per side

KNOWN TRUTHS REFERENCE CONVENTION:
  (0, 0) = bottom-left corner of FACE (web corner)
  Flanges extend into negative coordinates
  Face corner = (0,0), blank extends to (-ex, -ex) at lower-left

CONVERSION:
  Our blank coord = Known Truths face coord + (ex, ex)
  These are equivalent; our DXF draws correctly regardless of origin choice.


