SECTION 8 — COORDINATE GEOMETRY FORMULAS
================================================================================

FLAT PATTERN ORIGIN:
  Classic sheet metal: 0,0 at lower-left of flat sheet
  Software automation: 0,0 at lower-left of face/web (simplifies flange calculations)
  Our DXF: 0,0 at lower-left of blank (flanges extend inward from blank edge)

KEY VARIABLES:
  W, H     — finished outside width and height of panel face
  F1, F2   — flange depths (F1 = leg, F2 = lip/return)
  T        — material thickness
  R        — inside bend radius
  K        — K-factor
  BA       — bend allowance = (π/2)(R + K×T)
  OSS      — outside setback = R + T
  BD       — bend deduction = 2×OSS - BA

VERTEX INTERSECTION POINTS (corner notch locations):
  L4S:  L_total = F1 - OSS + BA  (from web edge)
  J4S:  L_total = (F1 - OSS) + (F2 - OSS) + (2 × BA)
  MIX:  X_vert = (F_side - OSS) + BA
        Y_vert = (F_top - OSS) + (F_ret - OSS) + (2 × BA)

NOTCH INTERSECTION COORDINATE (P_notch, face-relative):
  X: Px = -(Fs - OSS + BA)    [side flange]
  Y: Py = -(Ft - OSS + BA)    [top flange, L]
  Y (J-flange): Py = -[(F_leg1 - OSS) + (F_leg2 - OSS) + (2 × BA)]

BOOLEAN CORNER LOGIC:
  Miter corner (aesthetic/seamless):
    Condition: both adjacent flanges are J
    Miter_Gap typically 0.015" – 0.030" when explicitly used
    Current code default: gap = 0.0
    Result: nominal 45° diagonal cut line; if gap > 0 the apex opens slightly
    because the hard-corner-side endpoints move by gap/2 while the blank-edge
    endpoints stay anchored

  Overlap corner (structural/interlocking):
    Not implemented as a distinct overlap mode in current code
    Non-J+J corners terminate square instead of using a miter

PANEL TYPE CORNER SUMMARY:
  L4S: bend relief on perimeter at every active corner; no J miter
  J4S: both adjacent J sides mitered at 45° nominal; optional gap_override
       opens the apex slightly
  MIX (J/L): no miter at non-J+J corners; J+J miters where both sides are J
  2-side configs (J2TB/J2LR/L2TB/L2LR): square flange ends at active/inactive corners

BEND RELIEF (current generator):
  Perimeter-embedded square of side 2×T on bend-1 CL intersection; J+J keeps
  miter + five-point path; non–J+J uses quadrant + bridge to HC.
  (Legacy doc lines below — OSS + buffer face notch and separate back J circle —
  are shop intent; not drawn as extra entities in current DXF output.)

  Face notch depth/size = OSS + 0.010 buffer   [reference / optional future]
  Back J-relief diameter = 2 × T                 [reference / optional future]
  Back J-relief center = intersection of bend2 CLs at J+J


