  Software Rules (Fusion 360):
    Dynamic Radius: always set IR to match actual punch radius used in shop
    K-Factor: tight bends (R<T) use 0.33; standard (R=T) use 0.4469 baseline
    Successive bends: K-factor errors compound — test J-flange returns carefully

  Geometry Engine Rules:
    Face corner notch depth = OSS (self-scaling with thickness)
    Back J-relief radius = T (self-scaling)
    Tolerance buffer: add 0.010" to OSS for machine drift protection


SHOP NOTES — 6061-T6 ALUMINUM (use with caution):
  NEVER attempt tight bend (0.125" IR) on 6061-T6 thicker than 0.060"
  For 0.1875" thickness: 0.125" IR will almost certainly crack without annealing
  Minimum bend radius: 1.5T to 2.5T depending on temper
  Springback: significantly higher than 3003 — over-bend aggressively
    Use Data-M Laser Angle Tracking if available on machine
  Grain direction: cracking risk increases 30% when bending parallel to grain
  Recommended: always test on scrap of same lot before production run

SHOP NOTES — GENERAL:
  Anti-collision relief: shorten miter vertex ~1/32" for 0-relief J corners
  Square notch on face + circle relief on back = HD Clad system standard
  Square notch acts as architectural reveal feature when 4 panels meet
  Always verify flat pattern on first article before production run


